#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03125177-b036-57f5-a72a-3f4420748f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1+v+4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272411} {:answer/id #uuid "28abf496-f945-5a46-836c-05b71cb7c41f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272747} {:answer/id #uuid "6576c1eb-f6de-5994-856a-222b13c2c25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}{1+{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273255} {:answer/id #uuid "67a7dc74-a18e-510b-960e-2d9d5a7efdaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-v-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273280} {:answer/id #uuid "f3fe81de-e037-50b5-aa26-4a8e804b13c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272747} :answer-field/id #uuid "90700ab5-eeb4-56f3-8e94-25230b50b1ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f48980a9-f2e7-5b29-aaff-6351dbf19d07" :question/math-academy-id "q-14316" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-x(vx)+(vx)^{2}}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(1-v+{v}^{2})}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4240f0e5-b1a6-5f98-993e-7c328c878785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{y}{x}=C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272953} {:answer/id #uuid "62bc8038-4d46-561e-ab4d-c5512986257f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}|+2\\frac{y}{x}=C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273236} {:answer/id #uuid "78fcca57-3793-54d9-9ed6-e1885a1fdd95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273426} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed55e10-2aae-5111-b574-774642465adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273475} {:answer/id #uuid "aec77027-a6c4-54d9-8f83-8cb3685f4304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}|+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}=C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273896}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273475} :answer-field/id #uuid "729c88dd-5291-5373-98f6-d82abc2b83bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c139f739-608f-51ea-bcb4-01f8a92a8c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-14318" :question/problem "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)x}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{{v}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{2{v}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06801954-aceb-527f-87ea-95cb0f6de8cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}x-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272446} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca68fa9-62e4-5b19-b251-d7820af169fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272908} {:answer/id #uuid "610b5f06-7106-5295-bbce-136ddf73ac09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3xy+xy}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273225} {:answer/id #uuid "897cd727-6340-5a7f-a411-d1eec1449527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{{y}^{3}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273572} {:answer/id #uuid "94291e38-c665-530b-aa62-ffcb098f902f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273676}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272908} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb6e88a-8ce7-5065-891e-2b9f914a957e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc348cb6-a91b-542b-84f6-f5b771ae4157" :question/math-academy-id "q-14319" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $3.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $3-3=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)^{3}-3(tx)^{2}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{2}}{(ty)^{3}+(tx)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3})-{t}^{3}(3{x}^{2}y)+{t}^{3}(x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}({y}^{3}+{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275110 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d9fe79d-af55-52cc-807d-fdf8ff575196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273336} {:answer/id #uuid "7a705b5a-78f9-5bf4-bce8-236b06ad49a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273438} {:answer/id #uuid "83d1456f-a5d0-5b18-8867-aafba772b364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273519} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5879f0-7e3a-5185-9b2f-9e9609b66dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273742} {:answer/id #uuid "e17a8c50-895e-531b-acd7-eacf19bd14fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274376}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273438} :answer-field/id #uuid "35568be0-5728-557a-8bc2-7bde66432758" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "30f68eaf-916e-557d-ad03-5e30a2efe0b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-14321" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $3$ (i.e., they are cubic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}+x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)+{x}^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}({v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1)}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1-{v}^{3}-{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v+1}{v(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4875ea-48e5-5361-a8c6-15e5b78c5e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272504} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee30a5d-c60d-51de-8718-366ce9c6d7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x+y}{y}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272925} {:answer/id #uuid "6437d2a5-9b98-5547-b4b2-8979038ea84d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273247} {:answer/id #uuid "77c9d0da-c801-5a3a-a296-9ff45087e3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273408} {:answer/id #uuid "89bcafdd-55e6-5e96-9617-87e8ef808b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273574}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273247} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a0fc63-6ea7-5103-a6b4-659ab0b835cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9372b90-e355-5e25-8427-4c0e772f932c" :question/math-academy-id "q-14322" :question/problem "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}.$\n\nWe see that the numerator is NOT a homogeneous polynomial. Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is NOT a homogeneous function.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\nFor $x=1$, $y=2$ and $t=3$, for instance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =f(2\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =f(2,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{6}^{2}+2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{48}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =f(1,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}+1(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, there exists at least one combination of values of $x$, $y$ and $t$ for which the identity $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y)$ is not observed.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a81aecc-db87-5864-bf4a-a412676cae3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{1-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272896} {:answer/id #uuid "665d6fcb-2060-5376-afc2-497f1e6ffabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{3}+2{v}^{2}}{1-{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273264} {:answer/id #uuid "7e690b1e-0568-56f8-9cca-4a717d1758a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273470} {:answer/id #uuid "90821e35-81ef-5b74-b430-242af8a269fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{v+2}{1-3v-2{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273644} {:answer/id #uuid "cc67682d-4991-58c9-b814-c26b2c002615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1-2v-3{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274165}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273470} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcef863b-24d8-5be2-a251-e922d0413380" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "590e41cc-f7e5-52a9-8e4b-08ef663bf420" :question/math-academy-id "q-14323" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x(vx)^{2}-(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+2(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3})}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+2v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-2{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a0c82e4-a410-5545-aba6-e6bc3809dd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272760} {:answer/id #uuid "632f8488-1426-51de-b79c-859a00953830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273240} {:answer/id #uuid "8f09bfeb-fa40-5b8c-a65a-f33bf93f0996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273624} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa6a988-751b-5fc3-92dd-5e4dfbf0e530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273767} {:answer/id #uuid "df59ea5f-fed1-5499-abd7-c6c018da530f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274358}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274358} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a01516-b9bc-55d0-ac76-1962bc75b5ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c2654f6e-f38e-5fe7-bd83-e2905edb3c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-154357" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y}\n$$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{sec}^{2}⁡y} \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡y & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bcb38c3-d1e9-539a-b4e1-dab540d43230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272494} {:answer/id #uuid "658178ae-c54b-516e-b636-4665fc326043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273257} {:answer/id #uuid "74e2bd65-0d26-5b57-8915-d0995c4f7d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273386} {:answer/id #uuid "ab807a16-6387-5feb-ab59-267a4f6a3481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273867} {:answer/id #uuid "facac07e-06f2-51b9-b250-6d1ff2d92eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274586}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273386} :answer-field/id #uuid "465b078e-0db8-5efa-8088-98d975791b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c3a88f3-b655-5d1c-832a-8fe5b3af13b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-154361" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3K.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e68c45d-09d4-569c-b913-79d7d46d8f86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272658} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1adc60-82c0-5aa8-884b-65f615105a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272780} {:answer/id #uuid "42810437-8763-58f8-a94c-d08f4ca51719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272958} {:answer/id #uuid "88432955-bb9d-5cdb-8168-f7b9543320c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}={x}^{2}-2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273557} {:answer/id #uuid "a15158a7-e04f-5b2b-9783-52add73727d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272780} :answer-field/id #uuid "09996012-870f-5883-938b-a22328b3e885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e20f2fcf-b4a2-51d2-acda-66700b834327" :question/math-academy-id "q-154369" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{-y}(x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2{e}^{-y}(x-1) \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x & =\\int 2(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{2}-2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{e}^{y}={x}^{2}-2x+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb8f22b-8ca5-57ef-8370-d2d3c166b579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272810} {:answer/id #uuid "37747715-a217-5cdf-adc1-7537938bdbc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272874} {:answer/id #uuid "bf41e0ba-cb23-53f6-b183-adf43eec5717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274039} {:answer/id #uuid "d2409366-319f-54f1-9e94-19f43f971322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274225} {:answer/id #uuid "fadaeede-fe79-5093-a9c2-59e6513e62b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=\\sqrt{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274588}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274039} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06779cf-201b-5aa3-8047-f9fa3b7c1ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5b80541f-68bf-590f-9d99-5d43ea712334" :question/math-academy-id "q-154373" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sqrt{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{2{y}^{3/2}}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+K \\\\ {y}^{3/2} & ={x}^{3/2}+C \\\\ \\sqrt{{y}^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{3K}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}=\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275405 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053ca9da-737f-5368-b54e-24f96cafcde5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272436} {:answer/id #uuid "0bac610d-2d04-5604-ae64-cf06296f12ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272493} {:answer/id #uuid "41cc209a-81ce-50b5-9b00-4dc750c10cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272947} {:answer/id #uuid "c69d7489-94d3-50a5-a31f-01511961f376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274110} {:answer/id #uuid "fe66c8fc-fdf6-5a64-96a6-a35189bbdf14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-1/x}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274625}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274625} :answer-field/id #uuid "15153a99-fd23-5390-abfe-dedc4885900e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e0c7db14-c9c5-588a-b927-09334c1e0842" :question/math-academy-id "q-158009" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y=3$ for $y\\ne -3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y+3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y+3}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3|=-\\frac{1}{x}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y+3| & =-\\frac{1}{x}+C \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x+C} \\\\ |y+3| & ={e}^{-1/x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|y+3| & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y+3 & =K{e}^{-1/x} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{-1/x}-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275406 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e906697-63fe-5f9c-9695-47b9d1159642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272921} {:answer/id #uuid "491e2dd7-2197-5bca-8669-100af83cb2d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273009} {:answer/id #uuid "4a2b0b18-1859-5892-ace0-8191af79d18f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273016} {:answer/id #uuid "92ec8453-5e27-5368-9ac0-a98e23834e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273663} {:answer/id #uuid "b8730d08-4ef6-5d55-ade2-a86a1a24e46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273986}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273009} :answer-field/id #uuid "115fa6bc-8cbf-507c-a94a-1255297d1654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6f88ec76-892c-5986-98b6-3866ba9a8457" :question/math-academy-id "q-158010" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y=0$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,{y}^{′}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c59991-7a2a-5f22-a893-e1cd23ff3aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272993} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc9c947-fac1-5eb0-93a8-ce473b0e579a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273185} {:answer/id #uuid "6a59d67a-5461-5f00-bbb9-b66319e8bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273304} {:answer/id #uuid "71bcc40b-d574-5391-8487-43c9455497a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273364} {:answer/id #uuid "e4680ae6-1495-57dd-a494-1cc9894aadf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=(\\sqrt[3]{x}+C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274408}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272993} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ab142bb-121a-5834-81c7-b4ae5d3fdcbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "088db977-5f34-5d61-a165-97cdc5e6df38" :question/math-academy-id "q-158012" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019119ed-0828-5d14-913a-ecb47950b217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272395} {:answer/id #uuid "0b63defe-eba9-54f7-8c7f-b0bba025e804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272491} {:answer/id #uuid "612cc7e3-fab2-5707-b558-c6527bd1837a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273228} {:answer/id #uuid "83e2e646-4e20-564b-867b-ae7e68e0f341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273520} {:answer/id #uuid "a01c641c-59d0-5fde-8400-4b249323e3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273773}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272491} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdbfba5c-9780-5693-999b-a9c027c35c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "253f761f-d9dd-516e-a877-3691e4e75b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-158013" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e3c6b0-0e58-5c33-8744-40f2dcdff54e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272603} {:answer/id #uuid "78f4f93b-be8f-5c4d-a519-6d99d4fba770" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273424} {:answer/id #uuid "8883ebfa-4000-5edd-9354-c90407ee9c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273559} {:answer/id #uuid "952e6dd1-43ff-54f6-9de1-fd7289574d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273685} {:answer/id #uuid "e21a3412-a805-5477-baaf-507c3b52c7c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274386}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272603} :answer-field/id #uuid "379ffcc8-e905-5697-a128-ee6a8efb7a2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c6ab8c9-fca1-56b1-82a8-98c4fa9f8c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158014" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291a5622-7898-54ac-9d79-b2a74f3942f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272754} {:answer/id #uuid "319d04e8-d751-5e77-9108-47d7c52f477e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272832} {:answer/id #uuid "465f3293-d914-56fa-982c-5e0bcdc0476d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272987} {:answer/id #uuid "59934890-57e8-5e1f-8f0a-10c08ef2b159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273152} {:answer/id #uuid "cc14ee5c-23f4-50e2-8f50-91774b8a5ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274164}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272754} :answer-field/id #uuid "7709ba3d-848c-528e-ad97-e70bdde49520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4256446e-61ea-5cf5-ad92-3c95c9cc3119" :question/math-academy-id "q-158015" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168d25b1-5b64-5d3a-a2b7-c07ef0adf37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272587} {:answer/id #uuid "2e929ac6-a215-572b-81bc-05969c0d9468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272802} {:answer/id #uuid "424f3e94-8534-53b7-b3aa-7b4bef9b02b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{1/\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272954} {:answer/id #uuid "427309e1-eaaf-5f5c-8bf8-672f0974d1c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272957} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c3240e-d572-51cb-813a-ff9c0033b549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274437}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272957} :answer-field/id #uuid "75f19b13-10f3-5f7c-b83c-7f4d9aae5e0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ec2b6cd2-ba6d-52f7-9530-1a245bad9c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-158016" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $|x|<1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3089ac08-c20b-5f5f-8fde-8ef85e86835d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272818} {:answer/id #uuid "5193c1ee-640a-53fa-9486-21c5e01f0389" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273081} {:answer/id #uuid "6af3d8bf-0ef9-53e9-85b8-da693e7f5bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273308} {:answer/id #uuid "c058c6a7-887f-54ce-82c3-dd19e85fedb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274054} {:answer/id #uuid "f21cb61e-e665-5306-836b-7113089e955b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274525}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273308} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec8a4df6-eb47-5a40-a63c-fffc51d10f75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "594ba672-eefa-575c-8c38-2d0804124171" :question/math-academy-id "q-158017" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275414 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "494ae645-dd79-56e3-beb4-47a6995c7d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273011} {:answer/id #uuid "531a24d3-1d14-5b43-9a4f-2e858901dbc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273093} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd02c4a-ba52-56b7-a30a-66ebd3e84513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273339} {:answer/id #uuid "98601ac4-2a74-546e-8308-acabc08e7566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273709} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ffb26a-9163-59ae-8b17-526b2d86e380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273847}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273847} :answer-field/id #uuid "21ba5489-b345-5d21-a343-3f8e76c8cf24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c68a380-7f42-5c23-811b-3bce1cfeb2f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-158022" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y{e}^{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\cdot y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "498497a9-18b7-5c87-ba2a-a3d0a3acd277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273014} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccdbf3f-261a-5033-ad7a-fb8da9b4c6a4" :answer/type {:db/id 