parate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{3}^{2y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={3}^{x}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25050499-14a7-5dc4-ab9a-bb2746663571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272711} {:answer/id #uuid "31b1aac8-08aa-5f55-8a92-c7f2de5e3b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272834} {:answer/id #uuid "69ab19fa-2da0-5694-babc-dcaf4c1cbc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273297} {:answer/id #uuid "c86bbe3a-aa64-534f-b564-ff975b747ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{3}}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274129} {:answer/id #uuid "dd413836-9565-5ef5-855f-8525ec3a92ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{2}^{-x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274333}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272711} :answer-field/id #uuid "9311d56f-4976-5a5a-abe8-4574c024893b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "31bffd11-cf10-5855-9455-e621eb1969bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-158025" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{y}^{3}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275418 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511f2926-3a2d-5876-aadf-4d80c3a72b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273076} {:answer/id #uuid "542425f7-6cb3-5652-b4c4-c4e7fd2c0916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273105} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4f8557-52a4-5276-a1e1-4b5aaf1bd9f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273190} {:answer/id #uuid "8eb6ea03-73f9-5ab9-bec2-771fcf49b774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273623} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2a5003-9e7c-551d-aa36-6e3b23569a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274015} :answer-field/id #uuid "c987bfcc-3ddd-51b1-9ee6-0c54d27baf82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e87161c3-2cae-55f5-bb92-55f97a5739b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158026" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}{x}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28ef5c14-78d0-5208-855a-6b41a420438a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272752} {:answer/id #uuid "80fed0a8-073f-57d9-9a9b-52a42a33835b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\text{ }\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273493} {:answer/id #uuid "82123406-b934-5a9c-8160-0677d7d54cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273499} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e404da-fc1a-5a36-9bce-6763d8f34e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274086} {:answer/id #uuid "d122fedc-b019-5f58-8be1-37fe87dddc8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274209}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274209} :answer-field/id #uuid "e400646f-8ad1-5f1d-ad65-32dd857ca29e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c0d607e3-0c1a-5227-a757-1fdd9227cb73" :question/math-academy-id "q-158027" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b03335-77aa-59fa-b7e8-6e2269d546b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272397} {:answer/id #uuid "719ee0ff-8189-52e3-bc17-a3256803c517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273361} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2e38d7-f3bf-597e-9a67-9bf1f67d04c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273480} {:answer/id #uuid "a4697080-8561-5e7e-b488-d65e1a6352a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273806} {:answer/id #uuid "abf0e68e-bca8-580f-9a48-d359bd48f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273870}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272397} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ffe6dcc-9fa6-5228-9a8e-a4756f2ab21b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7037401f-27c0-588d-a952-7eb3ef7b14ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-158030" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71673ba5-a378-5710-9335-cc0008aef108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273358} {:answer/id #uuid "7d32ab15-cbb6-55a1-b112-149aeef16cab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5x+1}{3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273458} {:answer/id #uuid "893d3a4c-5ba0-5b1b-a19f-e339fc0dc9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5xy+y}{3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273570} {:answer/id #uuid "c621efd1-dd66-5976-9fe1-f299c7ad75bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x+1}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274106} {:answer/id #uuid "f01057d5-b998-5b8f-8b95-f2363bc35510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274513}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274513} :answer-field/id #uuid "e450d81c-8d75-511b-8599-f5fc6a521993" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe104c00-01e9-59b5-87fa-d82fed8f3827" :question/math-academy-id "q-158032" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5xy+y}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A differentiable equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differentiable equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3x}{(5x+1)y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x}{5x+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3x}{5x+1}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7988d84c-0ea4-5988-8ba2-c95a358645a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273430} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b829dd-2a25-59c2-94a0-d8a65efff454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\text{ }y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273853} {:answer/id #uuid "c09a28a4-9df6-5a65-b137-e6409c6a24dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y={x}^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274058} {:answer/id #uuid "c397d6c5-1419-560a-b38e-5dbaf38f637e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274085} {:answer/id #uuid "efb5eff8-9bff-5df3-93d8-810704b8cbff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274509}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273430} :answer-field/id #uuid "21509f54-1783-5348-95f3-0c5cd428b6f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "448a7a77-8f84-5ac7-87e1-3803e2799bbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-158035" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & ={x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡y={x}^{3}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c8a0d36-f6e2-5a0a-89e6-2d26ad013533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272639} {:answer/id #uuid "64177146-09d3-586f-a38e-d67e4b445b8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273246} {:answer/id #uuid "69ce8b4d-9357-5dca-8786-946b6bd0da61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273300} {:answer/id #uuid "8242ae78-fb2f-5486-ada7-1e349d52072c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273503} {:answer/id #uuid "c1de0088-404a-5b93-9e68-eab2a6e24abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡y=\\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274070}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186273246} :answer-field/id #uuid "96425cca-34f0-5837-934b-74d6042e90fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b0b5140d-8021-52c8-9880-109bb8e78b6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158116" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y}\n$$ for $x\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡y\\operatorname{tan}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d153f63-b757-54a0-920b-62e754969c14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272788} {:answer/id #uuid "56b00252-91b0-5b60-8e8f-804dca0617c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273126} {:answer/id #uuid "d4879ac6-9572-5560-9ee7-27001a2d76ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274251} {:answer/id #uuid "e9eae476-aba3-55b4-b017-91ac6b9a54ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274458} {:answer/id #uuid "fd235e72-e654-5d2c-b2d3-bbc9bacb1db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274610}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186274610} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a4727f-caa7-5dcd-91c3-adb929275f98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1c9d63db-85c4-5f46-a91d-0a91ded8b499" :question/math-academy-id "q-158117" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284499 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0890c131-5eeb-5f67-aa90-086374575a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281763} {:answer/id #uuid "18e0c24c-52d2-5c41-a933-2d13b3e8afa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281913} {:answer/id #uuid "1ebf50dd-9fc4-55fb-91d9-28de2bacb253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281964} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba9ca97-13f2-5cf7-9f0e-df8b3d876788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282614} {:answer/id #uuid "97883037-baea-5b8b-9a40-b05574105c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281913} :answer-field/id #uuid "63fe44b0-587e-52d7-9525-c7108d7f5367" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fdeb0ff5-45e6-5343-a0cd-f339e82d372b" :question/math-academy-id "q-16451" :question/problem "![](images/61/6116ecf00a26d9828b238879b61385c1296f33ff863dbb8337a3b22be5981f10.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
